Subject: delegate.c: stub system() on wasi, like Android/iOS already do

ImageMagick already ships a "this platform cannot run external programs" path
for iOS and Android:  #define system(s) ((s)==NULL ? 0 : -1).  wasm32-wasip1 is
in exactly that position, so reuse it instead of inventing a new one.  With
MAGICKCORE_HAVE_POPEN / _EXECVP / _FORK undefined (see
wasm/config/MagickCore/magick-baseconfig.h) the whole of
ExternalDelegateCommand() collapses to this stub, which returns -1 and makes
InvokeDelegate() raise a normal DelegateError exception.

--- a/MagickCore/delegate.c
+++ b/MagickCore/delegate.c
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@
   #if TARGET_OS_IOS || TARGET_OS_WATCH || TARGET_OS_TV
     #define system(s) ((s)==NULL ? 0 : -1)
   #endif // end iOS
-#elif defined(__ANDROID__)
+#elif defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__wasi__)
   #define system(s) ((s)==NULL ? 0 : -1)
 #endif
 #define DelegateFilename  "delegates.xml"
